er circuits","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:2a20a5b0af320d92b2c4d0e9214d8fbf66a232fd28fce0ee07a763b84224f914","file":"preprints/Finite-tensor-savings-and-exact-Fourier-circuits-September-25-2026/build/sections/03-fourier-transfer.tex","line":310,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"3f3c74a3f787a3c8d4a6387672262a1a4798214cd5d57d94af737d0fa719652b","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Finite-tensor-savings-and-exact-Fourier-circuits-September-25-2026/build/sections/03-fourier-transfer.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:2a20a5b0af320d92b2c4d0e9214d8fbf66a232fd28fce0ee07a763b84224f914","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Finite-tensor-savings-and-exact-Fourier-circuits-September-25-2026/build/sections/03-fourier-transfer.tex#L310"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:win-to-fourier}\nIf a finite win exists, there are integers $n_m\\to\\infty$ and exact\nlinear circuits for $F_{n_m}$ whose scalar gate counts satisfy\n\\[\n L(n_m)=o(n_m\\log_2n_m).\n\\]\nIn particular the conclusion is in the model charging additions,\nsubtractions, and multiplication by every prechosen complex scalar."}
